module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.ClassGame

/-!
# The game with cyclic classes excludes `00110011111111`, `0000000000111011` and `0000101111111001`

The finite game at 15 or 16 cells closes three blocks of period 14 and 16 that its surveys at widths up to 14 miss and
that nothing else in this repository or the kit excludes. The plain game's test is the class test's case in which the
left column is a function of the phase, and the phase is a function of the cyclic class, so [ClassGame](ClassGame.md)'s
certificates prove them: `class_column` holds for any block with a valid `ClassCert`. Each certificate is at the least
width at which the class test closes the block, 13 cells for `00110011111111` and 15 for the other two, made by
`computations/class_blocks_wide.py`.

For each block `b` there is one section with the certificate `cls<b>`, one kernel check per width and phase and one per
phase of the classes, and the theorems `column_not_<b>` (every column of every row with a leftmost 1),
`center_not_<b>` (the center column) and `not_eventually_<b>` (the kit's form).

The natural-language argument is `GameBlocksWide.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata
open Rule30StripCertificateTable (wordOf)

/-! ### The block 00110011111111 at 13 cells

Widths 1 to 13 check 28,134 nodes, with heights up to 39; the classes cover
the 8,574 nodes of height 0 at 13 cells, with 262 ranks and labels modulo 14 and 28. -/

